        <body>
            <div xml:id="d532">

                <pb facs="0593" n="481" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg481"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Fox to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-07-09"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">July 9, 1910</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 679.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor, respectfully referring to
                    my cablegram of July 2, to inclose herewith copies of notes, with translations,
                    exchanged between this legation and the minister of foreign relations, with
                    reference to the demobilization of troops in Ecuador and Peru; also copy of the
                    memorandum of a convention which Ecuador would be willing to sign with Peru in
                    the premises.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Williams C. Fox.</hi></signed></closer>





